pe change revealed by NMR spectroscopy (Oh et al. 1998, Whiteford et al. 2008). The resulting complex is able to bind protein kinase C alpha which is persistently activated in the absence of Ca2+ (Oh et al. 1997, Lee et al. 1998, Keum et al. 2004).", "literatureReference": [2682283, 2682229, 2682240, {"dbId": 2682231, "displayName": "Solution structure of a syndecan-4 cytoplasmic domain and its interaction with phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate", "title": "Solution structure of a syndecan-4 cytoplasmic domain and its interaction with phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate", "journal": "J. Biol. Chem.", "pages": "13022-9", "pubMedIdentifier": 9582338, "volume": 273, "year": 1998, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9582338", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 2682260, "displayName": "Structural and cell adhesion properties of zebrafish syndecan-4 are shared with higher vertebrates", "title": "Structural and cell adhesion properties of zebrafish syndecan-4 are shared with higher vertebrates", "journal": "J. Biol. Chem.", "pages": "29322-30", "pubMedIdentifier": 18753130, "volume": 283, "year": 2008, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18753130", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 2682242, "displayName": "Syndecan signaling: when, where and why?", "title": "Syndecan signaling: when, where and why?", "journal": "J. Physiol. Pharmacol.", "pages": "31-8", "pubMedIdentifier": 20083849, "volume": 60, "year": 2009, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20083849", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 2731120, "displayName": "Syndecan-4 proteoglycan cytoplasmic domain and phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate coordinately regulate protein kinase C activity", "title": "Syndecan-4 proteoglycan cytoplasmic domain and phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate coordinately regulate protein kinase C activity", "journal": "